00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.740
Our AI analysis is learning from valuation discipline patterns and adjusting entry filters

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:05.600
accordingly. Imagine you allocated 40% of your TFSA to Canadian equities last year because the dividend

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:11.640
tax credit felt like free money and the names were familiar. Your order filled cleanly yet the

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:18.880
TSX's 50% weighting in financials and energy left you exposed to exactly the sectors already tied

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:25.500
to your job and mortgage. The mechanism is simple. Canada represents roughly 3% of global market

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:32.800
cap. A 30-50% home allocation means you are structurally underweight US technology and healthcare

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:39.120
that have driven most of the past decades returns. Professionals always check their total geographic

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:45.780
exposure across all accounts before adding another Canadian bank or pipeline. The biggest mistake

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:52.860
with home bias is treating familiarity as diversification. Instead, calculate your true Canada weight

00:10:52.860 --> 00:11:00.400
including employer stock and real estate. Then cap the equity portion at 20-25% unless you have a

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:06.280
specific currency hedging thesis. Before we wrap, open your brokerage platform and pull up the

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:14.760
